  "arrangerNotes": "Pentatonic melody, so no accidentals to remove. Verified against the Wikipedia LilyPond score. 'we'll' is the same 6 as 'syne' (some session settings put it on the high 1 instead). Lyric line breaks follow the phrases; slurred notes in the score carry one syllable over two notes. Range low 5 to 6, minLayout 11 on both drums. Medium because of the dotted rhythms. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–5: Robert Burns (1788), as printed in The Poetical Works of Robert Burns, ed. Alexander Smith (1887), p. 249, from Wikisource (https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Poetical_Works_of_Robert_Burns/Auld_Lang_Syne), in Burns's Scots; as in verse 1 here, each line ends with the pickup word of the next line. The chorus (verse-1 wording) is sung after every verse; 'mony a' is sung as two syllables. Per-verse notes (verseLines): in verses 2, 4 and 5 the second line ends with a two-syllable pickup ('but we've', 'and we'll'), so its last quarter note is played as two eighths of the same pitch.",
  "verified": true
}
